      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "The question converts model no3 and po4 to micromoles per kilogram at a constant density, and this fragment states that CMIP6 BGC concentrations are stored per unit volume with variable-specific scale factors to the usual units.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`no3`/`po4` are archived in mol m-3: convert to µmol kg-1 as µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ with ρ in kg m-3; mmol m-3 (= µmol L-1) is still per volume, not per mass.",
        "The N:P ratio and its thresholds are invariant under scaling, so take them from the native per-volume fields; the question prescribes a constant ρ = 1025 kg/m3 for the µmol kg-1 regression (the fragment prefers in-situ density below the surface), so state the density used (`attrs['density_assumption']`) and that the difference is the question's choice."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "Comparing models with WOA23 and computing basin/global statistics requires a single valid-cell mask applied to all fields, which this fragment constrains.",
      "status": "not_applicable",
      "not_applicable_reason": "no cell-by-cell comparison across sources is asked; each source's regression, means and volume fractions are taken over its own valid cells, and the common frame is for display only."
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
