      "reason": "The question uses the WOA23 basin mask with marginal seas folded and Southern/Arctic basins excluded, and this fragment warns that basin statistics depend on the partition used and must be stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Basin means use the WOA23 mask (`select_basin`, `load_basin_mask`), the Ofx `basin` field being absent: state that mask was used, with marginal seas folded in (`include_marginal_seas=True`, as the question prescribes) and Southern and Arctic treated as separate basins and excluded.",
        "Use the surface labels through the whole column (`depth_dependent=False`) for a named ocean; a marginal sea's own label stops at its sill below that depth."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "The question uses each model's own volcello for the 200-1000 m layer and volume weighting, and this fragment defines volcello as tracer-cell volume and explains how layer thickness is recovered.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Take layer thickness for 200-1000 m as `volcello` / `areacello` (`cell_thickness_like`), not `lev_bnds` differences, which fail at partial bottom cells; GFDL-ESM4's `volcello` is monthly and must be used as such.",
        "Volume-weighted means and volume fractions use each model's own `volcello`; state the volume/area origin (`attrs['volume_source']`) behind any integral."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Global and basin means and percentage-of-water-volume statistics must be volume-weighted over all ocean cells rather than simple cell averages, as this fragment specifies.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Use `op='volume_weighted_mean'` over the layer, restricted to the same valid cells; the mean of the cell-by-cell N:P (`compute_ratio`) and the ratio of the two volume-weighted means are different quantities — report both, labelled.",
        "A volume percentage inside an N:P range is a volume share, not a share of cells: `compute_exceedance_fraction` keeps missing cells out of the denominator and returns the m3 behind the percentage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "The 1971-2000 climatologies are built from monthly CMIP6 time averages, and this fragment warns that offline nonlinear diagnostics such as N:P from monthly means differ from online diagnostics and from the mean of the diagnostic.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Average the monthly 1971-2000 fields with `temporal_aggregate` (day weights in the model calendar); `compute_basic_stat(op='mean', dim='time')` weights every month equally.",
        "N:P is nonlinear in monthly means, so state the order: \"average first, then diagnostic\" is the like-for-like choice against the WOA23 climatology; \"diagnostic first, then average\" gives the mean of the monthly ratios instead."
      ]
    },
